<title>AUSTRIA: Flughafen Wien up on Turkey project report.</title>
<headline>Flughafen Wien up on Turkey project report.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Vienna airport group Flughafen Wien rose on Wednesday on a report the company was part of a consortium awarded a $307 million contract to expand Istanbul's Ataturk airport, traders said.</p>
<p>At 1140 GMT Flughafen was up one schilling at 511 on heavy volume of 68,435 contracts. Earlier the stock had been trading around 508 schillings.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the firm could not confirm the report by Anatolian news agency that a consortium consisting of Turkey's Tepe and Akfen firms and Flughafen had won the project. -- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12257</p>
</text>
